    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like a lot of those \"safeguards\" end up being used as excuses to protect huge corporations that can afford the lawyers, while the little guys get crushed by the same rules. it almost feels like regulation is just a tool for the status quo. don't you think it's more accurate to say that most 'necessary' regulation is actually just an obstacle to a truly free and competitive market?, the way it market is actually, you wouldn period differentiate between",
